            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Add 4 to successive multiples of LCM(6, 7, 8) until the result is divisible by 5.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Subtracting 4 gives a common multiple of 6, 7 and 8.\n$$\\begin{align*}6&=2\\times3\\\\7&=7\\\\8&=2^3\\\\\\operatorname{LCM}(6,7,8)&=2^3\\times3\\times7\\\\\\operatorname{LCM}(6,7,8)&=168\\end{align*}$$\nAdding 4 to successive non-negative multiples of 168 gives $4,172,340,\\ldots$. The first multiple of 5 is $340$.\nCheck: $340=6\\times56+4=7\\times48+4=8\\times42+4$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
